{"v":1,"type":"session-summary","author_email":"contact@atkn.me","session":"kandev:83a0b430-49c1-4819-89d0-81c76deb6fd8","created_at":"2026-09-29T22:40:00Z","entries":[{"driving_event":"The ledger proved a repository could attest to a byte-reproducible checkpoint, but nothing could attest to who produced the evidence or to the checkpoint itself, so a compromised host could publish a self-consistent but unattributable history.","decision":"Add an immutable sg: signature record alongside the existing evidence records, sign the canonical eight-field manifest payload under a domain-separated digest, verify through an injectable SignatureVerifier port with an in-process ed25519 default, and require roles from the reveries.signingRoles configuration; ledger checkpoints carry a growing append-only signature log whose lines are never dropped or rewritten and whose newest content_id equals that manifest hash.","impact":"Every evidence or ledger record can now carry a cryptographic attestation, checkpoints are signed during build rather than after the fact, and a signature stays valid across a deterministic rebuild because the signed bytes are manifest-derived. Trust resolves to absent, unsigned, untrusted, trusted, or policy-satisfying with trust evaluated before the verdict, and a malformed role configuration surfaces as a doctor diagnostic instead of crashing.","recurrence_control":"76 new tests across protocol, trust, verifier, roles, rotation, and signed-checkpoint suites pin domain separation, the four trust states, the append-only carry-forward rules, role resolution and its override precedence, and key rotation. The committed tree was verified in isolation at 443/443 with the 348 RVR-005 baseline and no semantic payload function modified, and DESIGN.md section 27.3.2 records the contract.","alternatives":["Anchor signatures to immutable commit objects as a signed tag, so that Git itself carried the attestation.","Sign the whole manifest document instead of the canonical eight-field payload, trading a narrower and more stable contract for less explicit field-level control."],"sources":[{"relation":"implements","kind":"issue","ref":"github:phynics/reveries#9"}],"reveries":[],"retirements":[]}]}
